  "Guinea 2025: the USGS estimate of bauxite mined is 150 Mt, 34% of the world total, but Guinea's exports alone were reported at 182.8 Mt for 2025 (official data seen by Reuters, in Hellenic Shipping News, January 2026: https://www.hellenicshippingnews.com/guineas-bauxite-exports-jump-25-to-183-million-tons-in-2025-on-chinese-demand/), more than USGS estimates Guinea mined; the same article gives 74% of the shipments to China (Chinese customs data). The USGS production figure and Guinea's share of the world total are therefore probably understated.",
